"[2609.21670] Centro-affine spectral geometry of polytopes (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.21670)\nciteturn6view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.21670\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Metric Geometry\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 18 Sep 2026]\nL9: # Title:Centro-affine spectral geometry of polytopes\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Yingxiang Hu , cite6†Mohammad N. Ivaki L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Centro-affine spectral geometry of polytopes, by Yingxiang Hu and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:In this paper, we develop a polyhedral version of Milman's centro-affine spectral framework for full-dimensional origin-symmetric polytopes. A weighted graph Laplacian on the facets plays the role of the smooth centro-affine Laplacian. For $n\\geq 3$, we prove that its first nonconstant even eigenvalue satisfies \\[\nL17: > \\lambda_{1,e}(P)\\geq n-1+\\frac{1}{n-1} \\] whenever $P$ is a local minimizer of $\\lambda_{1,e}$ among origin-symmetric polytopes with the same facet normals, but not necessarily the same normal fan.\nL18: Subjects:  | Metric Geometry (math.MG); Analysis of PDEs (math.AP)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2609.21670 [math.MG]\nL20:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2609.21670v1 [math.MG] for this version)\nL21:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.21670†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Mohammad Ivaki [cite12†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:06:32 UTC (42 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the p